### VULN-011 — CORS unanchored regex + credentialed origin reflection (config-gated)

### Precondition (admin, supported ACP settings):
PUT /api/v3/admin/settings/access-control-allow-origin-regex   {"value":"example\\.com"}
PUT /api/v3/admin/settings/access-control-allow-credentials    {"value":"true"}

### Attacker probe (UNAUTHENTICATED; a real attack runs this from an attacker web page with credentials:'include'):
GET /api/config HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21372
Origin: https://example.com.attacker.net
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) Chrome/124.0.0.0 Safari/537.36

# -> HTTP/1.1 200 OK
#    Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://example.com.attacker.net    <-- attacker origin reflected (unanchored match)
#    Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true                           <-- credentialed cross-origin read allowed
#    (body includes csrf_token when the request carries the victim's cookie)

### Control (origin without the 'example.com' substring) — NOT reflected:
GET /api/config HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21372
Origin: https://unrelated-evil.org
# -> (no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header)
